    "instagram:post": {
      "caption": {
        "body": "#Onthisday in 1958, Pan American World Airlines received the first of eight Boeing 707-120s. This Boeing 707-121, the \"Clipper Maria\", was the last 707 delivered to PanAm in 1958. The 707 was developed by Boeing as the result of an initial 1955 request from Pan American for a large jet-powered airliner. The jet’s speed and passenger capacity enabled the airline to substantially reduce their seat-mile costs, thus lowering ticket prices and open up air travel to a larger percentage of the public. As a result of its efficiency, the 707 proved to be the world’s first truly successful commercial jetliner with consistent, sustained scheduled service. Have you ever flown on a Boeing 707?  Image: Roll-out of Pan American World Airways’ Boeing 707 Jet Clipper, 1958. Gift of William E. Talbott. 2012.151.153",
